          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em category of fibrant objects
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            equipped with extra structure somewhat weaker than that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          %p
            The extra structure of fibrations
            %em and
            cofibrations in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            is, while convenient if it exists, not carried by many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
            which nevertheless admit many constructions in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            A
            %em category of fibrant objects
            is essentially like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            but with all axioms concerning the cofibrations dropped, the concept of fibrations retained (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+category"}> fibration category
            ”) and assuming that all objects are fibrant (whence the name). It turns out that this is sufficient for many useful constructions. In particular, it is sufficient for giving a convenient construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            in terms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+cohomology+theory"} homotopical cohomology theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong category of fibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi W
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Core(\mathbf{C}) \hookrightarrow W \hookrightarrow C
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Mor(W)
                  is called a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %strong weak equivalence
              %li
                %p equipped with a further subcategory
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi F
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi C
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Core(\mathbf{C}) \hookrightarrow F \hookrightarrow C
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Mor(F)
                  is called a
                  %strong fibration
            %p
              Those morphisms which are both weak equivalences and fibrations are called
              = succeed "." do
                %strong acyclic fibrations
            %p This data has to satisfy the following properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  has
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*}
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  of a fibration along an arbitrary morphism exists, and is again a fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  acyclic fibrations are preserved under
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %li
                %p
                  weak equivalences satisfy
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              %li
                %p
                  for every object there exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path object
                %ul
                  %li
                    this means: for every object
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                    there exists at least one object denoted
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^I
                    (not necessarily but possibly the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                    with an
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi Id
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Id
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi σ
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi I
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            (B \stackrel{Id \times Id}{\to} B \times B)
                            \=
                            (B \stackrel{\sigma}{\to} B^I \stackrel{d_0 \times d_1}{\to} B \times B)
                    %p
                      where
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                      is a weak equivalence and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0 \times d_1
                      is a fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  all objects are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em fibrant
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to {*}
                  to the terminal object are fibrations.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#FullSubcategoriesOfModelCategories Full subcategories of model categories
          %p
            The tautological example is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            on all objects which are fibrant.
          %h3#RightProperModelCategories Right proper model categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            be the class of weak equivalences, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_+
            be the class of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is also a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            together with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_+
            satisfy all the conditions to be a category of fibrant objects
            %em except
            possibly the condition that every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_+
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of those objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            is in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_+
          %p
            For example,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            via its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} standard model structure
            is a category of fibrant objects in this way. The fibrations in this case are not the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            (these also yields a category-of-fibrant-objects structure, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfModelCategories"} the above
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+maps"} sharp maps
          %h3#groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Groupoids
          %p
            This includes notably all models for categories of
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                = succeed "es" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-groupoid"} strict omega-groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+strict+omega-groupoids"} model structure on strict omega-groupoids
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complexes
              form a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} Brown category of fibrant objects
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path object
              of any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              can be chosen to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^I = [\Delta^1, X]
            %p
              in with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              with the simplicial 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X^I
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} degeneracy map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_0 : \Delta^0 \to \Delta^1
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    [\Delta^0, X]
                    \\stackrel{[\sigma_0, X]}{\to}
                    [\Delta^1, X]
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is indeed a weak equivalence, since by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
              it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              (a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} right inverse
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Delta^1, X] \stackrel{[\delta_0,X]}{\to}
                    [\Delta^0, X]
                    \\,.
            %p
              This map, one checks, has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} right lifting property
              with respect to all
              = succeed "-inclusions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary of a simplex
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta^n \to \Delta^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\delta_0,X]
              is an acyclic fibration. Hence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\sigma_0, X]
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            %p
              The remaining morphism of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path space object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^I \to X \times X
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ⊔
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Delta^1, X]
                    \\stackrel{[\delta_0 \sqcup \delta_1, X]}{\to}
                    [\Delta^0 \sqcup \Delta^0, X]
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    X \times X
                    \\,.
            %p
              One checks that this is indeed a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            %p
              The stability of fibrations and acyclic fibrations follows from the above fact that both are characterized by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} right lifting property
              (as described a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %p
              See for instance
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.abdn.ac.uk/~bensondj/papers/g/goerss-jardine/ch-1.dvi"} section 1
              of
            %ul
              %li
                Goerss, Jardine,
                %em Simplicial homotopy theory
                \.
          %p
            Concerning the example of
            = succeed "es," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            is also a
            %em category of co-fibrant objects
            (i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SSet
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet^{op}
            is a category of fibrant objects) so that
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            But then, often it is useful to model Kan complexes using the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
          %h3#simplicial_sheaves Simplicial sheaves
          %p
            The point of the axioms of a category of fibrant objects is that when passing from
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            with values in
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "wise)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
          %p
            One can get around this by employing a more sophisticated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure as described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoid valued sheaves)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
              is an isomorphism precisely if its image
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x^* f : x^* A \to x^* B
            %p
              is a bijection of sets for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"}> geometric morphism
              s from
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh({*}) \simeq Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mo *
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x : Set \simeq Sh({*})
                    \\stackrel{\stackrel{x^*}{\leftarrow}}
                    {\stackrel{x_*}{\to}}
                    Sh(C)
                    \\,.
            %p Then let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi SSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{C} = SSh(C)
            %p
              be the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  with values in the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                  of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %li
                %p
                  equivalently:
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              on those sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              for which each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* A \in SSet
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %p
              Define a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              to be a fibration or a weak equivalence, if on each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* f : x^* A \to x^* B
              is a fibration or weak equivalence, respectively, of Kan complexes (in terms of the standard
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            %strong Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              For instance for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              we may take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Op(X)
              to be the
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The points of this topos precisely correspond to the ordinary points of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Equipped with its structure as a category of fibrant objects, simplicial sheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are a model for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
            %strong
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (the way an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh(X)
            is a sheaf “over
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Or let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                be a (small model of) the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                of smooth
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n
              %p
                Equipped with its structure as a category of fibrant objects, simplicial sheaves on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
                are a model for
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stack"} smooth infinity-stack
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(X)
              with this structure is a category of fibrant objects.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The terminal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} = X
              is the sheaf constant on the 0-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              itself as a sheaf.
            %p
              For every simplicial sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              of the unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to {*}
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* A \to x^* {X}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* A
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              for every
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a fibrant object by the above definition.
            %p
              The fact that fibrations and acyclic fibrations are preserved under pullback follows from the fact that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              operation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi SSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x^* : SSh(X) \to SSh(pt) \simeq SSet
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              and hence preserves finite
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              is a fibration or acyclic fibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
