                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper model categories
            %p Right properness is a crucial assumption in the closely related work
            %ul
              %li
                Jardine,
                %em Cocycle categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0605198"}> arXiv
                )
          %h3#homotopy_fiber_product Homotopy fiber product
          %p
            Using the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path space objects
            one can construct specific
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %em homotopy fiber products
            \.
          #HomotopyFiberProducts.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong homotopy fiber product
              or
              %strong homotopy pullback
              of two morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi u
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi v
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \stackrel{u}{\to} C \stackrel{v}{\leftarrow} B
            %p
              in a category of fibrant objects is the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times_C C^I \times_C B
              defined as the (ordinary)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
